  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The AI Horizon & The Observable Control Plane. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 33: Stuart Halloway from SCNA 2013 (2013).",
  "Stuart Halloway's SCNA presence connected the Chicago craftsmanship community with the emerging functional programming renaissance.",
  "Why did Clojure and Datomic capture the imagination of Midwest craftsmen seeking refuge from object-oriented ceremonies? What principles guided Stuart Halloway when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: eJtP70a6c2E). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Immutable append-only facts and temporal event logs are the foundation of observable agent telemetries and memory layers. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
